    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Clinic-Receptionist-Administrative-Assistant_JR105659": {
      "title": "Clinic Receptionist/Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout The Team Our Chiropractic team is part of Murdoch University's School of Allied Health and is committed to delivering high-quality, evidence-based chiropractic education. We are a collaborative team of clinicians, educators and professional staff who support students through hands-on learning, supervised clinical practice in our on-campus clinic, and community outreach initiatives. We foster a supportive, professional and student-centred environment, preparing graduates with the skills, professionalism and collaborative approach needed to thrive in diverse healthcare settings. Your New Role!  This is not your typical clinic reception role. As part of a busy teaching clinic, you'll work in an environment where no two days are the same, supporting both clinic operations and student learning. We're looking for a confident, organised and adaptable administrator who enjoys variety, takes initiative and can confidently manage competing priorities. You'll also play an important role in guiding students in reception and administrative processes. As the Clinic Reception and Administration Officer, you will work closely with the Clinic Manager to provide high-quality reception and administrative support, coordinate clinic activities and contribute to a positive experience for patients, students and staff. The position is rostered across Monday and Wednesday from 7.00am to 3.30pm (including a 30-minute meal break), Tuesday (5 flexible hours) and alternate Saturdays from 7.30am to 4.00pm (including a 30-minute meal break). Flexibility is essential, as clinic operating hours may vary from year to year and may involve early starts, later finishes and occasional additional hours to provide leave coverage and support clinic operations. While the roster pattern may change in 2027, the fortnightly hours will remain consistent. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Continuous, Part time (25 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $82K – $91K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.   You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: A relevant Associate Diploma qualification or equivalent experience and training. Exceptional communication and relationship-building skills. Strong organisational skills and the ability to balance competing demands while maintaining attention to detail. The ability to take initiative, work independently and collaborate effectively as part of a team. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite.   Ability to safely perform Incidental manual handling tasks associated with the role Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Abbey Chilcott, Academic Lead, Clinical Education, A.Chilcott@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105659 as the reference. Applications Close on 14 September 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Meet-Murdoch-Team-Assistant_JR105150": {
      "title": "Meet Murdoch Team Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout The Team The Meet Murdoch Team is part of our multi‑channel Future Student Service Centre, supporting Murdoch University’s 10‑year strategy for significant student growth. We engage domestic and international prospective students through phone, email, online chat, SMS and face‑to‑face interactions on campus and at major career expos and education fairs. Your New Role!   We are seeking multiple casual Meet Murdoch Team Assistants to support future student engagement and Admissions operations. In this role, you’ll deliver high‑quality customer service across a range of enquiries and assist the Admissions Team with efficient application processing and communication. Your key responsibilities will include: Respond to inbound enquiries from domestic and international future students via phone, email, online chat, and face‑to‑face. Support outbound calling campaigns to future and current students. Convert future student enquiries into applications through clear, supportive communication. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This casual role attracts a competitive casual rate of $42 p/hr – $46 p/hr inclusive of 25% casual loading plus 12% employer superannuation contributions.   You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Strong telephone manner with excellent verbal and written communication skills. Confident in engaging with a diverse range of callers in a professional and welcoming way. Proven ability to build rapport, influence prospects, and convert enquiries into student applications. Demonstrated discretion and professionalism when handling confidential information. Proficient in the Microsoft Office suite with strong accuracy in data entry. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check and have a valid working with children check or the ability to register for one in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Jacky Julies, Co-ordinator, Future Student Enquiry, j.julies@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105150 as the reference. Applications Close on 13 September 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Bioinformatics-Analyst_JR105446": {
      "title": "Bioinformatics Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Personalised Medicine Centre is a collaborative research partnership Murdoch University and the Perron Institute, bringing together leading researchers and clinicians and to advance personalised medicine. The Centre focuses on developing innovative treatments tailored to individual patients based on their unique genetic makeup and lifestyle. Our research spans a range of critical health challenges, including genetic therapies, genomics, motor neurone disease, sepsis, immunogenomics, drug hypersensitivity, cognitive health, muscular dystrophy, and neurodegenerative disorders such as Parkinson’s disease, myositis, and multiple sclerosis. Your New Role!   A key objective of the University’s Research and Innovation Strategy is to provide the resources needed to support research excellence. The establishment of a central medical genomics facility will strengthen Murdoch’s nationally and internally recognised, fully accredited genomics capabilities, enhancing research and teaching across disciplines. The Bioinformatics Analyst will primarily support the Drug Hypersensitivity Research Group, which investigates severe immune (T-cell)-mediated adverse drug reactions, including Stevens-Johnson syndrome and toxic epidermal necrolysis (SJS/TEN). The group's research spans the discovery of genetic (HLA) risk markers for prevention through to the integrated analysis of single-cell transcriptomic, T-cell receptor (TCR), and metabolomic data to improve diagnosis and treatment. The successful candidate will contribute to cutting-edge medical genomics research by developing, applying, and supporting bioinformatics tools and workflows, and by delivering analytical expertise across both population-scale and single-cell multi-omics datasets. Your key responsibilities will include – Analyse and interpret genomic, transcriptomic, and proteomic/metabolomic data using advanced bioinformatics tools and techniques Develop, maintain, and support bioinformatics pipelines, while providing training and guidance to researchers and users Ensure analyses meet accreditation standards and best practice, maintaining expertise in emerging bioinformatics technologies and methodologies   Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (2 Years) | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a starting salary of $93k (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.  The position is also eligible for salary step progression within the classification level in accordance with Murdoch University's Enterprise Agreement. You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Bachelor of Science Degree in Molecular Biology, Computational Biology, Computer Science, or a related discipline or an equivalent combination of qualifications and experience Strong knowledge of bioinformatics principles, with proficiency in programming languages such as Python or R Experience developing and implementing bioinformatics analysis workflows and pipelines Understanding of sequencing technologies and their application in life sciences research Excellent communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively with researchers, clients, and multidisciplinary teams   Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Andrew Gibson, Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Andrew.Gibson@murdoch.edu and quote JR105446 as the reference. Applications Close on 11 September 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Philanthropy-Manager---Engagement_JR105315": {
      "title": "Philanthropy Manager - Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Alumni & Philanthropy Office is a collaborative and dedicated team committed to driving the University’s philanthropic vision. Together, they lead and deliver a wide range of initiatives, including major gifts, bequests, endowments, annual giving, capital campaigns and corporate and foundation grant programs, while ensuring thoughtful and impactful donor stewardship. The team works closely with alumni, donors and the broader community, creating meaningful connections through engaging communications, events and programs. Their shared focus is on building strong, lasting relationships that inspire giving and strengthen the University’s community. Your New Role!   As the Philanthropy Manager – Engagement , you'll play a key role in strengthening relationships with donors and showcasing the impact of philanthropy at Murdoch University. Working closely with donors, alumni, and internal stakeholders, you'll deliver meaningful engagement initiatives that inspire ongoing support and create lasting connections with the University. In this role, you will: Develop and deliver donor engagement, stewardship, and recognition programs.  Build and manage meaningful relationships with an allocated portfolio of donors. Create impactful donor communications, reporting, events, and engagement activities. Please refer to the Candidate Pack for further details. What We Offer You! This Continuous, Full Time (37.5 hours per week) position attracts a remuneration of $116K – $133K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (Found in the position description in the Candidate Pack) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Relevant tertiary qualifications and minimum five years’ experience, or equivalent Proven experience building and managing meaningful donor, alumni, or stakeholder relationships. Exceptional written communication skills, with the ability to create engaging donor-focused content. Strong project management and event coordination skills, with a keen eye for detail. A collaborative mindset and the ability to manage multiple priorities while delivering outstanding stakeholder experiences. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record in accordance with the University's Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Brooke Webb, Senior Philanthropy Manager, Brooke.Webb@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105315 as the reference. Applications Close on 17 September 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
