    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Associate-Professor-in-Small-Animal-Surgery_JR105260": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer or Associate Professor in Small Animal Surgery",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Our Small Animal Surgery team provides specialist referral services across soft tissue, oncologic, orthopaedic and neurosurgical cases. Due to the upcoming retirement of one of our long-standing Professors, we have two positions available in our surgery team for either Soft Tissue or Orthopaedics focussed or someone who enjoys all aspects of surgery. The team consisting of two board certified surgeons, one residency trained surgeon, three residents and two Post Graduate Trainees (interns) brings together extensive surgical expertise to support pets with a wide range of complex conditions, from abdominal, thoracic and cardiovascular procedures through to advanced orthopaedic, spinal and reconstructive surgery. Working within a fully equipped hospital environment, the team is supported by specialist anaesthesia, 24-hour intensive care, internal medicine, oncology, cardiology, advanced diagnostic imaging, clinical pathology laboratory and highly skilled nursing staff. This integrated approach allows the service to manage challenging surgical cases while maintaining a high standard of care before, during and after surgery. The team works closely with referring veterinarians to provide advice, consultation and surgical treatment tailored to each patient’s needs. Whether a case is straightforward or highly complex, their focus is on delivering expert surgical care and supporting a smooth recovery through coordinated postoperative management with the pet’s regular veterinarian. Your New Role!   The Animal Hospital at Murdoch University stands out as a leading veterinary centre in Western Australia, offering a diverse caseload, advanced diagnostic facilities, and a collaborative environment. As part of a prestigious university, you’ll work alongside world-class specialists and contribute to teaching and research, ensuring continual professional growth. Our commitment to excellence, innovation, and compassionate care creates a unique learning culture where both new graduates and experienced veterinarians thrive. You’ll join a supportive, friendly team dedicated to clinical excellence and personal wellbeing. We provide structured mentorship programs, ongoing training, and opportunities to participate in groundbreaking research. Competitive compensation and a strong focus on professional development make The Animal Hospital at Murdoch University an ideal workplace for passionate veterinary professionals seeking both career advancement and community. Position Descriptions Senior Lecturer Associate Professor What We Offer You! Renumeration, Visa Sponsorship and Relocation is negotiable. You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: A degree in Veterinary Science registrable with the Veterinary Surgeons’ Board of Western Australia A clinical specialist qualification (DECVS, DACVS or fellowship) in small animal surgery. Demonstrated ability to work under broad direction only, exercise initiative in undertaking responsibilities and work effectively as a team member. A high level of achievement in successfully supervising honours, Masters by Coursework, HDR and postgraduate students (including residents) to completion. A record of success in the application of curriculum design and pedagogy, including substantial experience with leading and designing programs of study. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Visa sponsorship and relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Henry Annandale, Dean of Veterinary Medicine, henry.annandale@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105260 as the reference. Applications Close on 16 October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Agricultural-Science-Teaching-and-Learning-Talent-Register_JR105577": {
      "title": "Agricultural Science Teaching and Learning Talent Register",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nAbout The Team The School of Agricultural Science at Murdoch University is shaping the future of agriculture through excellence in teaching, research and industry engagement. Our teaching and learning activities prepare graduates to address challenges in food and fibre production, animal health and biosecurity. We deliver undergraduate and postgraduate degrees, together with research training programs. Our coursework offerings include majors in: Animal Science Animal Health Crop and Pasture Science Biosecurity Food Security The team also delivers minors in Equine Science and Agribusiness. Our teaching and learning programs combine strong foundational knowledge with hands-on learning through laboratories, fieldwork and industry placements, equipping students with the skills and networks needed for careers in modern agriculture, animal health and biosecurity. About the opportunity We invite expressions of interest from candidates with relevant academic and/or industry experience to join our teaching talent register for casual and fixed-term opportunities within the School of Agricultural Science. Lectures Workshops, laboratory classes and field-based teaching activities Tutorials Marking Animal handling demonstration involving horses, cattle, sheep and pigs We welcome applications from both experienced educators and industry professionals who can bring contemporary knowledge and real-world perspectives to student learning. Please register for the talent pool online via the Apply Now button. The following documents should be submitted to support your application: A cover letter that includes: an outline of your areas of expertise and relevant experience subject areas and teaching activities of interest availability for face-to-face teaching at the Murdoch University South Street Campus and/or online delivery Your most recent resume (CV) detailing academic qualifications, teaching experience and relevant professional industry experience This Talent Register will remain active until 31st August 2027 Candidates whose skills and experience align with emerging teaching needs may be considered for casual or fixed-term teaching opportunities as they arise. Please note: successful candidates may be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Visa sponsorship is not available for positions that will be filled from this talent register. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity please reach out to agscience@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105577 as the reference. Applications for this talent register close on 31 August 2027 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    }
  },
